<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44930" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spectātrix</span></b> ,
		īcis, f.
		spectator. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>She that looks at</i> or <i>observes</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Merc. 3, 4, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 2,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Cons. ad Marc. 18 <i>med.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 2,
				12, 26</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scelerum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					3, 129</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>She that judges</i> or <i>tries</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incorrupta praeteritorum (posteritas),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 30, 8, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humanorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 22, 3, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spectatrix dijudicatrixque omnium rerum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Dogm. Plat. 2, p. 15, 23</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
